*==============================================================================
* OPAMP_FULL  -  behavioural op-amp macromodel (PSpice port)
*
* Copyright (c) 2026 Stanislav Maslovski
* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause  (see LICENSE)
* Version 1.4 (2026-11). Developed with the help of Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).
* PSpice port, generated by tools/make_pspice_port.py from ../opamp_full.lib.
* Do not edit by hand: change the main library and run the script again.
* Same pins, parameters and behaviour as the main library (checked against
* ngspice with tests/cross_sim.py). Tested with PSpice 9.1 (1999 evaluation
* version), so it should also run in later PSpice releases. Differences:
*   - B sources and parameter-gain E/G/H sources are E/G VALUE={} sources;
*     ?: is IF().
*   - VCMN defaults to 1e30, which means mid-supply (PSpice 9 cannot default a
*     parameter to an expression of other parameters).
*   - PSpice differentiates VALUE expressions numerically. To keep the small-
*     signal results exact, the output-stage command current is carried in mA
*     (nicmd...), the crossover input in mV (nvx...), and the clamp excesses on
*     their own nodes (nex...). 1e15 ohm partners give the 1k noise references
*     the two connections PSpice requires.
*
* Pins: inp inn vcc vee out
*
* LINEAR EFFECTS
*   - finite DC gain A0, dominant pole, GBW, two extra poles (FP2, FP3)
*   - differential / common-mode input R and C (noiseless)
*   - CMRR and PSRR(+/-) with frequency roll-off (a zero in the coupling gain)
*   - output resistance (ROUT) and output capacitance
*   - input voltage noise (white + 1/f) and input current noise (white + 1/f,
*     FCIN = current-noise 1/f corner, independent on each input; 0 = off)
* NONLINEAR EFFECTS
*   - input offset voltage, input bias and offset currents
*   - input stage tanh() characteristic  -> slew rate and large-signal THD
*   - optional separate rising / falling slew rates (SRR, SRF)
*   - optional follower jump from the input-pair tail capacitance (KJUMP)
*   - input common-mode range (gm collapses near the rails)
*   - optional differential input clamp: anti-parallel diodes between inp
*     and inn (VCLMP, RCLMP); no clamps to the rails
*   - output voltage swing limited by the supplies (VHD/VLD headroom)
*   - output current limit (ISRC/ISNK), class-AB crossover dead-zone (VXO)
*   - supply current = quiescent + load current drawn from the right rail
*
* Defaults approximate a general-purpose 1 MHz bipolar op amp on +/-15 V
* (uA741-like typicals). Rail-to-rail example parameters are given at the end.
*
* Units: SR in V/s (0.5Meg = 0.5 V/us). PSRR/CMRR as ratios (31.6k = 90 dB).
*
* Notes
*   - VOS, the input voltage noise and the CMRR/PSRR error terms form one
*     error voltage in series with the + input, ahead of RID (RID is driven
*     by the internal V(vd)). So no spurious (VOS+en)/RID current flows in
*     the source resistance.
*   - All model-internal resistors are noiseless (VCCS form), except the
*     1e15 ohm leak resistors (negligible noise). The only noise
*     generators are Rnv, Rnp, Rnn (white), Dfa (1/f voltage) and Dfp1, Dfn1
*     (1/f current, FCIN > 0). Noise levels are
*     exact at TEMP = 27 C and scale like kT elsewhere.
*   - Portability (v1.3): tested in ngspice-42 and LTspice 26 (identical
*     DC/AC/transient/noise results). White e_n is passed through the E
*     source Ewn (LTspice ignores the noise of a resistor that is read only
*     inside a B-source expression). Nodes that otherwise see only G
*     elements and capacitors get a 1e15 ohm DC path to ground (R*lk), which
*     satisfies the floating-node checks of LTspice/PSpice; their effect on
*     gain and noise is negligible. This file is the PSpice port.
*   - Bias currents: IB > 0 flows INTO the pins (NPN input); use IB < 0 for PNP.
*   - RIC || CIC is the common-mode input impedance of EACH input pin to
*     ground (per-pin datasheet values, e.g. "34 Mohm, 4 pF each input").
*     With both inputs tied together the impedance is RIC/2 || 2*CIC.
*   - VCMN: the input common-mode voltage at which VOS is specified. The CMRR
*     error term is (Vcm - VCMN)/CMRR. The default is mid-supply.
*   - Differential clamp: two anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn, each
*     with forward voltage VCLMP at 1 mA and
*     series resistance RCLMP. The default VCLMP=100 disables it (the 741 has
*     no clamp diodes; leakage < 1e-14 A at 15 V). For an OP27-style clamp use
*     VCLMP=0.7 RCLMP=100 (the original model's DIN diodes).
*   - Crossover: for |Iout| << VXO/ROUT the small-signal output resistance is
*     2*ROUT. It is ROUT once |Iout| > ~2*VXO/ROUT (2 mV/75 ohm ~ 50 uA).
*     Set VXO=0 for a plain ROUT everywhere.
*
* PARAMETERS  (name, unit, default, meaning)
*  Gain and frequency response
*   A0      V/V    200k     open-loop DC gain
*   GBW     Hz     1Meg     gain-bandwidth product (unity-gain frequency of the
*                           dominant-pole response)
*   FP2     Hz     3Meg     second pole
*   FP3     Hz     10Meg    third pole
*   SR      V/s    0.5Meg   slew rate (0.5Meg = 0.5 V/us)
*   SRR     V/s    0        slew rate of the rising (positive-going) output;
*                           0 = SR
*   SRF     V/s    0        slew rate of the falling (negative-going) output;
*                           0 = SR. LF155 datasheet pulse photo: SRR ~5.5Meg,
*                           SRF ~11Meg
*   KJUMP   -      0        input-pair tail capacitance: output jump / fast
*                           input common-mode step (large-signal follower
*                           response); 0 = off. The sign gives the input-pair
*                           polarity: > 0 npn/nmos (jump on rising edges),
*                           < 0 pnp/pmos/p-JFET (jump on falling edges).
*                           uA741 (datasheet pulse response): KJUMP ~0.27
*                           with the default SR
*  Input DC errors and impedance
*   VOS     V      1m       input offset voltage, in series with the + input
*   IB      A      80n      input bias current (average of the two pins);
*                           IB > 0 flows into the pins (NPN), IB < 0 out (PNP)
*   IOS     A      20n      input offset current, I(inp) - I(inn)
*   RID     ohm    2Meg     differential input resistance (noiseless)
*   CID     F      1.4p     differential input capacitance
*   RIC     ohm    400Meg   common-mode input resistance of each input pin to
*                           ground (noiseless)
*   CIC     F      0.75p    common-mode input capacitance of each input pin to
*                           ground
*  Differential input clamp (two anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn;
*  there are no clamp diodes from the inputs to the supply rails)
*   VCLMP   V      100      forward voltage of each diode at 1 mA (set through
*                           the emission coefficient); 100 = no clamp.
*                           OP27-style clamp: VCLMP=0.7 RCLMP=100
*   RCLMP   ohm    100      series resistance of each clamp diode
*  Common-mode and supply rejection
*   CMRR    ratio  31.6k    DC CMRR (31.6k = 90 dB)
*   FCMRR   Hz     200      CMRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency
*   PSRRP   ratio  31.6k    DC rejection of the positive supply
*   PSRRN   ratio  31.6k    DC rejection of the negative supply
*   FPSRR   Hz     100      PSRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency
*   VCCN    V      15       nominal positive supply (PSRR reference)
*   VEEN    V      -15      nominal negative supply (PSRR reference)
*   VCMN    V      mid      input CM voltage at which VOS is specified; the
*                           CMRR error is (Vcm - VCMN)/CMRR
*  Noise
*   ENOISE  V/rtHz 20n      white input voltage noise density
*   FCEN    Hz     200      1/f corner of the voltage noise
*   INOISE  A/rtHz 0.5p     white input current noise density, each input
*   FCIN    Hz     0        1/f corner of the current noise (independent on
*                           the two inputs); 0 = white only
*  Supplies, input range and output swing
*   ICCQ    A      1.7m     quiescent supply current, vcc to vee
*   ICMHI   V      2        input CM range: distance below vcc at which the
*                           input-stage gm has fallen to half (< 0: beyond rail)
*   ICMLO   V      2        the same, above vee
*   VK      V      0.15     width of the gm roll-off at the input-range edges
*   VHD     V      2        minimum headroom, output to vcc (swing limit)
*   VLD     V      2        minimum headroom, output to vee (swing limit)
*  Output stage
*   ROUT    ohm    75       output resistance
*   COUT    F      3p       output capacitance to ground
*   ISRC    A      25m      maximum source current
*   ISNK    A      25m      maximum sink current
*   VXO     V      2m       class-AB crossover dead zone: for |Iout| below about
*                           VXO/ROUT the small-signal output resistance is
*                           2*ROUT; 0 disables it
*==============================================================================

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* ZCPL : out = K * (1 + s/(2*pi*FZ)) * in      (ideal zero, exact derivative)
* Used for CMRR(f) and PSRR(f): coupling into the input rises above FZ,
* i.e. the rejection ratio falls at 20 dB/dec. FHI limits the derivative.
* The derivative resistor is a noiseless VCCS.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt ZCPL in out PARAMS: K=1u FZ=1k FHI=20Meg
.param TAUZ={1/(6.283185307*FZ)} CD=1n
Ek na 0 VALUE={(K)*V(in)}
Cd  in nx {CD}
Gd nx nv VALUE={(6.283185307*FHI*CD)*V(nx,nv)}
Vs  nv 0 0
Rlk nx 0 1e15
Ed out na VALUE={(K*TAUZ/CD)*I(Vs)}
.ends ZCPL

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt OPAMP_FULL inp inn vcc vee out
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=200k GBW=1Meg SR=0.5Meg SRR=0 SRF=0 FP2=3Meg FP3=10Meg
+ VOS=1m IB=80n IOS=20n
+ RID=2Meg CID=1.4p RIC=400Meg CIC=0.75p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=200 PSRRP=31.6k PSRRN=31.6k FPSRR=100 VCCN=15 VEEN=-15
+ VCMN=1e30
+ ENOISE=20n FCEN=200 INOISE=0.5p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=1.7m VHD=2 VLD=2 ICMHI=2 ICMLO=2 VK=0.15
+ ROUT=75 ISRC=25m ISNK=25m VXO=2m COUT=3p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100 KJUMP=0

* ---- derived constants -------------------------------------------------------
.param PI2=6.283185307
.param VCMX={IF(VCMN>1e29, 0.5*(VCCN+VEEN), VCMN)}   ; VCMN=1e30: mid-supply
.param C1V=30p
.param SRRV={IF(SRR>0, SRR, SR)}
.param SRFV={IF(SRF>0, SRF, SR)}
.param IMAXV={0.5*(SRRV+SRFV)*C1V}  ; mean input-stage current limit -> slew rate
.param IDIFV={0.5*(SRRV-SRFV)*C1V}  ; half the difference (asymmetric slew)
.param GM0={PI2*GBW*C1V}           ; small-signal transconductance -> GBW
.param R1V={A0/GM0}                ; DC gain A0 = GM0*R1V
.param VNTH={sqrt(4*1.380649e-23*300.15*1e3)}   ; thermal noise of 1k at 27C
* 1/f source: diode biased at IFL. Its flicker voltage density is
* KF*IFL*(Vt/IFL)^2/f = KF*Vt^2/(IFL*f), so KF = ENOISE^2*FCEN*IFL/Vt^2.
* The two diodes also add white shot noise 2*(2*q*Vt^2/IFL), i.e.
* (0.21 nV/rtHz)^2 at 10 mA. It is subtracted from the white generator so
* that the total white density is exactly ENOISE (for ENOISE > 0.21 nV).
* (IFL much above 0.1 A upsets the transient time-step control.)
.param IFL=10m
.param VTN={1.380649e-23*300.15/1.602176634e-19}
.param KFV={ENOISE*ENOISE*FCEN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param ESH2={4*1.602176634e-19*VTN*VTN/IFL}
.param GENV={sqrt(max(ENOISE*ENOISE-ESH2,0))/VNTH}
.param GNI={INOISE/VNTH}
* 1/f current noise (FCIN > 0): one more flicker diode pair per input, so the
* two pins get independent noise. The flicker voltage of the pair is scaled to
* VNI*sqrt(FCIN/f) with VNI = 1 uV/rtHz and converted to current by GFI =
* INOISE/VNI, giving INOISE^2*FCIN/f. The pair's shot noise then adds only
* (0.21n/1u)^2 = 4e-8 of INOISE^2. FCIN = 0 disables the sources (GFI = 0).
.param KFI={1e-12*FCIN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param GFI={IF(FCIN>0, INOISE/1u, 0)}

* ---- input network (noiseless) -------------------------------------------------
* RID carries V(vd)/RID, i.e. it sits behind the series error voltage
* (VOS, noise, CMRR/PSRR), as if that voltage were in series with the + pin
Gid inp inn VALUE={(1/RID)*V(vd)}
Cid  inp inn {CID}
Gic1 inp 0 VALUE={(1/RIC)*V(inp)}
Gic2 inn 0 VALUE={(1/RIC)*V(inn)}
Cic1 inp 0 {CIC}
Cic2 inn 0 {CIC}
* bias currents flow INTO the pins for IB > 0 (NPN input)
Ibp  inp 0 DC {IB+IOS/2}
Ibn  inn 0 DC {IB-IOS/2}
* optional differential input clamp diodes: VCLMP = diode drop at 1 mA
* (set via the emission coefficient), RCLMP = series resistance
Dp1  inp inn DIN
Dp2  inn inp DIN
.model DIN D(IS=1e-15 N={VCLMP/(VTN*log(1e-3/1e-15))} RS={RCLMP})

* ---- noise sources (visible to .noise analysis only) ------------------------
* white voltage noise: thermal noise of a 1k resistor scaled by GENV in Ewn
Rnv  nnv 0 1e3
Rnv2 nnv 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnv
Ewn nwn 0 VALUE={(GENV)*V(nnv)}
* white current noise on each input
Rnp  nnp 0 1e3
Rnp2 nnp 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnp
Rnn  nnn 0 1e3
Rnn2 nnn 0 1e15   ; PSpice: second connection at nnn
Gnp 0 inp VALUE={(GNI)*V(nnp)}
Gnn 0 inn VALUE={(GNI)*V(nnn)}
* 1/f voltage noise: flicker noise of a diode biased at IFL, minus an
* identical KF=0 diode so that the DC drop cancels
Ifa  0 nfa DC {IFL}
Dfa  nfa 0 DFLK
Ifb  0 nfb DC {IFL}
Dfb  nfb 0 DQ
Efl  nfl 0 nfa nfb 1
.model DFLK D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFV} AF=1)
.model DQ   D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* 1/f current noise, independent on each input (FCIN > 0)
Ifp1 0 nfp1 DC {IFL}
Dfp1 nfp1 0 DFLKI
Ifp2 0 nfp2 DC {IFL}
Dfp2 nfp2 0 DQ
Gfp 0 inp VALUE={(GFI)*V(nfp1,nfp2)}
Ifn1 0 nfn1 DC {IFL}
Dfn1 nfn1 0 DFLKI
Ifn2 0 nfn2 DC {IFL}
Dfn2 nfn2 0 DQ
Gfn 0 inn VALUE={(GFI)*V(nfn1,nfn2)}
.model DFLKI D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFI} AF=1)

* ---- CMRR and PSRR coupling into the input -----------------------------------
Ecm ncm0 0 VALUE={0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-VCMX}
Xcm  ncm0 ncm ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/CMRR} FZ={FCMRR}
Eps1 nps1i 0 VALUE={V(vcc)-VCCN}
Xps1 nps1i nps1 ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRP} FZ={FPSRR}
Eps2 nps2i 0 VALUE={V(vee)-VEEN}
Xps2 nps2i nps2 ZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRN} FZ={FPSRR}

* ---- effective differential input voltage ------------------------------------
* = V(inp) - V(inn) + series error voltage (VOS + CMRR/PSRR terms + noise)
Evd vd 0 VALUE={V(inp)-V(inn)+VOS+V(ncm)+V(nps1)+V(nps2)+V(nwn)+V(nfl)}

* ---- input common-mode range window (0..1, 0.5 at the ICMR edge) ---------------
Ewin nwin 0 VALUE={max(0.25*(1+tanh((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-V(vee)-ICMLO)/VK))*(1+tanh((V(vcc)-ICMHI
+ -0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))/VK)),1e-3)}

* ---- input-pair tail capacitance (KJUMP) ----------------------------------------
* The tail (common) node of the input pair follows the higher (KJUMP > 0,
* npn/nmos) or lower (KJUMP < 0, pnp/pmos) input (Solomon, IEEE JSSC 1974).
* TPL = sign(KJUMP). When a fast input step drives the tail, its charging
* current u = TPL*I(Vtl) > 0 is
* steered to the gain node, so the output of a follower jumps by |KJUMP| times
* the input step (in the uA741 the charge reaches the joined bases of the
* lateral pnps through an emitter-base junction, with current gain). On the
* other edge the tail follows the output slowly; its discharge current is
* small and is not modelled (u < 0 is ignored). Only input common-mode motion
* matters: a resistive inverter shows a smaller effect (its summing node moves
* while the output slews); small-signal analyses are unaffected.
.param TPL={IF(KJUMP<0, -1, 1)}
.param KTC={max(abs(KJUMP),1e-12)}
Etl ntl0 0 VALUE={0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))+(0.5*TPL)*sqrt((V(inp)-V(inn))*(V(inp)-V(inn))+2.5e-3)}
* Ctl has a noiseless series resistance (time constant 1/(2*pi*FP3)): the
* sensed current is then a smooth state, not the step-to-step ringing that
* trapezoidal integration gives in a capacitor driven by an ideal source
* (the max() below would rectify that ringing).
.param RTL={1/(PI2*FP3*KTC*C1V)}
Vtl  ntl0 ntl 0
Gtl ntl ntlc VALUE={(1/RTL)*V(ntl,ntlc)}
Ctl  ntlc 0 {KTC*C1V}
Rtllk ntlc 0 1e15

* ---- input stage + dominant pole (tanh gives slew limiting) ------------------
* The current limit IL = IMAXV + IDIFV*tanh(4*GM0*vd/IMAXV) moves smoothly from
* SRF*C1V (vd < 0) to SRR*C1V (vd > 0) well before the tanh saturates, so the
* output slews at SRR up and SRF down. The small-signal gm stays GM0 at vd = 0
* (IL cancels to first order); with SRR = SRF the stage is the plain tanh.
Ggm 0 n1 VALUE={tanh(GM0*V(vd)/(IMAXV+IDIFV*tanh((4*GM0/IMAXV)*V(vd))))*((IMAXV+IDIFV*tanh((4
+ *GM0/IMAXV)*V(vd)))*V(nwin)+max(TPL*I(Vtl),0))}
G1 n1 0 VALUE={(1/R1V)*V(n1)}
C1   n1 0 {C1V}
R1lk n1 0 1e15
* soft clamp of the gain node to the swing limits (fast overdrive recovery)
Ehi nhi 0 VALUE={V(vcc)-VHD}
Elo nlo 0 VALUE={V(vee)+VLD}
Eex0 nex0 0 VALUE={V(n1)-V(nhi)}
Eex1 nex1 0 VALUE={V(n1)-V(nlo)}
Gclp n1 0 VALUE={(IMAXV/1e-3)*(max(V(nex0),0)+min(V(nex1),0))}

* ---- higher-order poles (noiseless 1k / C sections) --------------------------
G2   0 n2 n1 0 1m
G2r  n2 0 n2 0 1m
C2   n2 0 {1/(PI2*FP2*1e3)}
R2lk n2 0 1e15
G3   0 n3 n2 0 1m
G3r  n3 0 n3 0 1m
C3   n3 0 {1/(PI2*FP3*1e3)}
R3lk n3 0 1e15

* ---- output stage ----------------------------------------------------------------
* Norton output: I = (V(n3)-V(out) with crossover dead-zone)/ROUT, hard-limited
Evxmd nvxmd 0 VALUE={1e3*(V(n3)-V(out))}   ; vx in mV
Eicmd nicmd 0 VALUE={1e3*min(ISRC,max(-ISNK,((1e-3*V(nvxmd))-0.5*VXO*tanh((1e-3*V(nvxmd))/(VXO 
+ +1e-9)))/ROUT))}
* smooth split into source (from VCC) and sink (to VEE) currents:
* Bsrc - Bsnk = Icmd exactly, and the slope is well-defined at I = 0
Gsrc vcc out VALUE={0.5e-3*(V(nicmd)+sqrt(V(nicmd)*V(nicmd)+1e-6))}
Gsnk out vee VALUE={0.5e-3*(sqrt(V(nicmd)*V(nicmd)+1e-6)-V(nicmd))}
Iq   vcc vee DC {ICCQ}
Cout out 0 {COUT}
.ends OPAMP_FULL

*==============================================================================
* Example parameter sets (use with  X1 inp inn vcc vee out OPAMP_FULL PARAMS: ...)
*
* Generic CMOS rail-to-rail, 5 V single supply, 5 MHz, 5 V/us:
*   A0=100k GBW=5Meg SR=5Meg FP2=15Meg FP3=50Meg VOS=2m IB=1p IOS=0.5p
*   RID=1T CID=2p RIC=2T CIC=1.5p CMRR=10k FCMRR=1k PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k
*   FPSRR=1k VCCN=5 VEEN=0 ENOISE=15n FCEN=1k INOISE=0.1f ICCQ=1m
*   VHD=0.05 VLD=0.05 ICMHI=-0.1 ICMLO=-0.1 VK=0.05 ROUT=100 ISRC=40m
*   ISNK=40m VXO=0 COUT=2p
*   (RIC=2T / RID=1T are fine; the Gmin of the simulator dominates.)
*   VCMN defaults to 2.5 V here (mid-supply).
*==============================================================================
